// Title: Shared Mailbox - SendAs/SendOnBehalf Activity (Baseline Visibility)
// Description: Returns every instance of a user sending as, or on behalf
//   of, a mailbox they don't own. Not an anomaly detection by itself - this
//   is the foundational inventory query for shared-mailbox usage. Run it
//   first to understand what legitimate delegate relationships exist in
//   your tenant (support rotations, EA-to-executive delegation, etc.)
//   before tuning the companion first-time-pairing and volume-anomaly
//   queries, and to spot-check unfamiliar sender/mailbox pairs manually.
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1098.002 (Account Manipulation: Additional Email Delegate
//   Permissions)
// Data source: Microsoft 365 Unified Audit Log, Sentinel's OfficeActivity
//   table, RecordType "ExchangeItem"
// False positives: N/A - this is a visibility/inventory query, not a
//   detection. Expect high volume in orgs with active shared-mailbox use;
//   filter to specific mailboxes of interest (e.g. finance@, hr@) for
//   focused review.

OfficeActivity
| where RecordType == "ExchangeItem"
| where Operation in ("SendAs", "SendOnBehalf")
| where UserId !~ MailboxOwnerUPN
| project TimeGenerated, Sender = UserId, SharedMailbox = MailboxOwnerUPN, Operation, ClientIP, ClientInfoString
| order by TimeGenerated desc
